    "narrative": "Today\u2019s slate is dictated by the high-stakes matchup against Misiorowski, a formidable arm whose 2.35 xERA severely dampens the offensive ceiling for **Will Smith**. While **Will Smith** remains in the lineup due to his premium slotting at #3 and a solid 0.389 xwOBA, his efficiency score of 48.91 reflects the difficulty of facing a sub-3.00 xERA starter. We are operating with a skeleton crew today, as the remainder of our core\u2014including **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**, **Cal Raleigh**, **Bryce Harper**, and **Lawrence Butler**\u2014are all idle due to team off-days. With our high-ceiling talent sidelined, the focus shifts to maximizing the few opportunities we have to accrue counting stats in a low-volume environment.\n\nIn analyzing the rest of our roster, **Justin Crawford**, **Daulton Varsho**, and **Tyler Freeman** remain on the periphery of active consideration, but with the lack of favorable platoon splits or exploitable park factors elsewhere, we are exercising extreme caution regarding game caps. **Yainer Diaz**, **Jonathan Aranda**, and **Matt Chapman** occupy the bench alongside **Dylan Beavers**, **Gleyber Torres**, and **Zack Gelof**, as none possess the elite sprint speed necessary to overcome the general inefficiency of today\u2019s projected offensive output. **Luis Arraez**, **Masyn Winn**, and **Brendan Donovan** were evaluated, but their potential impact on AVG is offset by the lack of stolen base upside against today's defensive alignments. \n\nThe closest decision today involved **JJ Bleday** and **Jung Hoo Lee**, both of whom narrowly missed the cut behind **Will Smith**. **JJ Bleday** was considered for his on-base profile, but the lack of a strong BvP advantage rendered the move marginal. Furthermore, **Jeremiah Jackson**, **Gavin Sheets**, **Kyle Karros**, **Alex Freeland**, and **Braden Montgomery** remain locked on the bench to preserve our caps for more favorable matchups later in the week. Given the volatility of the current weather reports and the elite caliber of the opposition's starter, we are prioritizing the preservation of our daily cap quota over forced participation in a high-risk, low-reward environment.",
